## Why This Is Asked

This question probes a candidate's ability to design a robust, privacy-preserving streaming system with practical API design, data modeling, and real-world constraints (late arrivals, auditing, fault tolerance).

## Key Concepts

- Secure aggregation in streaming systems
- Tamper-evident append-only logging
- Late-arrival handling and fault tolerance
- Differential privacy budgeting in continuous streams
- API design for edge-device contributions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: verify and accumulate a batch of shares securely
function processBatch(batch){
  const maskedSum = batch.shares.reduce((a,s)=>a + s.maskedValue,0);
  // server-side de-masking happens with stored keys
  return unmask(maskedSum);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate device keys without interrupting service?
- How would you detect and mitigate poisoned shares in real time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cross-region, multi-vendor aggregation pipeline with tamper-evident auditing and model_versioning. It checks API design, data modeling, robust aggregation, and rollout/rollback in production.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-region data ingestion and weighting
- Poisoning resistance and drift detection
- Versioning, canary rollouts, rollback
- Auditability and security controls

## Code Example
```javascript
function trimmedMean(arr, trim=0.1){
  const sorted = arr.slice().sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const n = sorted.length;
  const k = Math.floor(n * trim);
  const sliced = sorted.slice(k, n - k);
  return sliced.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0) / sliced.length;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor region skew and detect collusion? 
- How would you validate a rollback doesn’t impact older clients or data streams?

## Why This Is Asked
The new angle tests practical budgeting under load: how privacy budgets govern when DP noise is applied and when fast heuristics must be used, with per-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts
- Per-user privacy budgets and token-bucket refills
- Adaptive scoring paths and deterministic fallbacks
- Tenant isolation and budget accounting
- Conversational testing for budget enforcement

## Code Example
```javascript
// Mock budget check
function canSpend(userId, needed, store) {
  const remaining = store.getBudget(userId);
  if (remaining >= needed) {
    store.setBudget(userId, remaining - needed);
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

